DMM protocol library
====================

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

This Arduino-independent C++ library is an adaptation of the protocol and BLE
transport definitions in dmm-tools by Antoine Cellerier and contributors:
https://github.com/antoinecellerier/dmm-tools

Pinned upstream revision: 2d4dc507dbd6fa33b05b0241b368572f0ca15745
Retrieved: 2026-11-09

Adapted source paths under crates/dmm-lib/src:
  protocol/ut61eplus/{mod.rs,mode.rs,tables/*}
  protocol/ut171/{mod.rs,parse.rs}
  protocol/ut181a/{parse.rs,command.rs}
  protocol/ut80x/mod.rs (UT71 A/B and C/D/E layouts only)
  protocol/owon/{model.rs,decode.rs,decode15.rs,frame.rs,frame15.rs}
  protocol/zotek/{frame.rs,glyph.rs,layout.rs}
  protocol/bm78xbt/{packet.rs,decode.rs,tables.rs,login.rs}
  protocol/eevblog121gw/{packet.rs,decode.rs,tables.rs}
  protocol/framing.rs
  transport/ble/{profile.rs,issc.rs,fff0.rs,owon.rs,brymen.rs,eevblog121gw.rs}

Tests adapt the original projects' packet examples, real golden captures and
annunciator cases. Their provenance is preserved in the test fixtures and
compatibility document. Worked examples are labeled as such; they are not
local hardware captures.

Changes in this port: fixed-size, allocation-free C++ API, model registry,
output arrays with explicit channels, unit strings paired with values, bounded
stream buffering, portable host verification, and startup command metadata.
The library does not include the upstream simulators, GUI, USB transports,
remote button/control APIs or logging-memory interfaces.

